.SH NAME
messq-verify - check a data directory's invariants


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq verify [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the invariant checker over a messq data directory and report each check
as ok, violated or skipped.

.PP
verify works on a stopped directory, a live one, or a backup copy,
and answers "is my broker's state sound?" in seconds. Its exit codes
(0 clean, 1 violations found, 2 usage, 3 directory missing, 7 not
permitted) are part of the crash-harness contract.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for verify


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq verify --data-dir /var/lib/messq --deep
.EE


